  "body": "On the configured project cloud node 29609d47ba8e, exact source 00061b6 passed tests with the fixed nightly but failed strict Clippy on chunks_exact_to_as_chunks. Four fixture readers now use the array-chunk iterator. The production no_std codec and all golden bytes remain unchanged.\n\nThe mutation runner also needed a reproducible toolchain selection: a Cargo rustup-proxy path alone does not preserve a repository selection inside temporary crates. It now explicitly propagates --toolchain/RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN, records actual Cargo/rustc identities before every compile and test, and rejects missing, timed-out or drifting identities. All 15 baseline/mutant suites match one reference compiler. Schema v3 preserves the same 12 source mutants.\n\nA new single entry, tests/abi/run_acceptance.py, reads the existing upstream toolchain pin, resolves and hashes installed tools, snapshots executable inputs, runs every acceptance check, compares discovered test names/counts with actual execution and verifies unchanged source/fixture hashes. It does not install or fall back to another toolchain. Six acceptance-runner and seven mutation-toolchain tests enforce missing-tool, denominator, skip/filter, snapshot, overwrite, timeout and identity-drift failure behavior, including under Python -O.\n\nThe earlier part of this PR also closes nine proven old-suite survivors: capability-generation canonical equality, QueryAbi supported-operation dependencies and payload minima, and ReadUsage legal zero/full cap, exact elapsed consumption and aligned-window boundaries. It includes 19,404 capacity pairs checked independently in Rust and Python. Identical mutated-source hashes prove the old/new-suite controls differ only in coverage.\n\nActual final single-entry acceptance on cloud 29609d47ba8e:\n- Fixed nightly-2026-07-21: rustc 1.99.0-nightly (87e5904f5 2026-07-20), Cargo 1.99.0-nightly.\n- 13/13 complete acceptance checks; zero unexecuted checks.\n- Rust: 69/69 unit/integration + 1/1 doctest, zero failed/ignored/filtered.\n- Python: normal and -O each 46/46; independent Python mutation oracle 9/9, zero failure/error/skip.\n- Independent golden generators: 12/12 original, 24/24 edges, 1/1 transport.\n- rustfmt, strict all-target Clippy and x86_64-unknown-none no_std: pass.\n- Compiled mutation baselines: 8/8, 12/12, 7/7. Actual compiled mutants: 12/12 killed with 17 designated expected assertion failures; no compiler error, timeout, ignore or filter counts as a kill.\n- Actual compiler identities match before all 15 compilations and tests; original executable source/fixture hashes match before/after.\n- README.md remains 0 bytes; no new dependencies.\n\nHEAD 606244b6109b1060b4916baa76e3fdd14dcc5240 has parents 00061b6bd0886e393e5ea4113ff999e15ed47bfd and actual checked main bc294f75bfb8c03d9963f5a12ea23b9589779d96. The workflow, status and Hepta documentation are preserved byte-for-byte from that main. All 17 files different from main are A02-owned; there is no independent A02 edit to another owner's files. The verified local tree was compared with the GitHub-created tree before committing and immediately pushing without force.\n\n[Configured-cloud closure record](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/trillionnium-os-desktop/blob/agents/A02-hos2-wire/tests/abi/A02_CLOUD_CLOSURE_2026-10-16.md) includes exact invocation, resolved tool paths and the finite blocker inventory. Full logs and hashes: tests/abi/results/cloud-pinned-{before,acceptance,mutations}-2026-10-16.json. Existing profile and identical-source controls remain committed.\n\nReproduce with already provisioned fixed tools:\npython3 -B tests/abi/run_acceptance.py --rustup <existing rustup> --output-dir <new evidence directory>\nSet CARGO_HOME/RUSTUP_HOME for the installed project toolchain as documented. The existing source-mutation runner remains independently callable with --toolchain nightly-2026-07-21.\n\nThe three identified A02 code/host-execution blockers are closed. GitHub Actions dispatch issue #33 remains external: audited run 38930013313/job 117071289244 was queued, conclusion=null, not passed. The owned record provides a concrete A00 CI invocation without changing its workflow, required checks or security settings.\n\nNo shared Wire ABI or new protocol decision changed. HOS2 remains experimental major=2/minor=0; original consumed=35ms/33ms and post-demotion over-cap purpose are unchanged. A03/A05 consume the same Request/Response, explicit codecs, transport snapshot preflight, correlated response validation and ordered ID helpers. Published ioctl numbering, other architecture profiles and actual kernel/A05/A06/Hepta integration remain open; no syscall, user-copy, authorization, CPU enforcement or durable-owner acceptance is inferred from host tests.",
